/**
 * @mainpage Introduction
 ChibiOS - Copyright (C) 2006-2026 Giovanni Di Sirio.
 *
 * <h2>Features</h2>
 * - Object-oriented Hardware Abstraction Layer (XHAL), drivers are classes
 *   deriving from a common base driver class.
 * - Driver models for: ADC, CAN, Crypto, DAC, EFL, ETH, GPT, I2C, I2S, ICU,
 *   PAL, PWM, RTC, SDC, SIO, SPI, ST, TRNG, USB, WDG, WSPI.
 * - Complex drivers: Managed Flash Storage, MMC over SPI, Serial over USB,
 *   Serial NOR flash, sensors.
 * - Runtime selection among multiple driver configurations.
 * - Optional registry of the drivers instances.
 * - Driver interfaces and common code generated from XML descriptions.
 * - The drivers can be ported to virtually any MCU architecture thanks to
 *   an high level API.
 * .
 * <h2>Related pages</h2>
 * - @subpage concepts
 * .
 */
